            <ArticleTitle>Pseudo-aneurysm of the aortic root in a patient with mechanical aortic prosthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>797-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a case of an ex-intravenous drug user, who received mechanical valve prostheses in the aortic and mitral position for Staphylococcus aureus endocarditis and developed a pseudo-aneurysm of the aortic root with major peri-valvular regurgitation one year after surgery. The images of the transesophageal echocardiogram are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
